config MTK_CONSYS_BT
	bool "MediaTek MT6853 consys Bluetooth (/dev/stpbt)"
	depends on MTK_CONSYS_WMT
	default n
	help
	  The /dev/stpbt character device used by the vendor Bluetooth HAL:
	  H4 HCI packets carried over the WMT/STP core. The chip is powered
	  and the Bluetooth firmware is started when the node is opened and
	  powered down again on the last close. Nothing happens at boot, and
	  nothing at all unless the kernel command line has mtk_consys.hw=1.

	  The node is only created once the vendor wmt_loader has initialised
	  the connectivity drivers. mtk_stpbt.enable=0 on the kernel command
	  line keeps the node from being created.

	  If unsure, say N.
